     Setting this option will replace any configuration of `tradable_balance_ratio`.
 
+#### Limit exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that share the same underlying (base) currency - for example several
+altcoins that are all quoted against the same stake currency - a large adverse move in that
+currency can affect several of your open trades at the same time. `max_currency_exposure` lets you
+cap the total stake committed, across all simultaneously open trades, to a single underlying
+currency, as a fraction of your total tradable capital.
+
+For example, with `max_currency_exposure=0.2` (20%), the bot will never let the combined stake of
+all open trades whose pair shares an underlying currency exceed 20% of the total tradable capital.
+When opening (or increasing the size of) a trade would push that combined exposure above the
+limit, the stake amount for that trade is reduced to fit under the limit - the same way stake
+amounts are already reduced to fit `max_stake_amount` or the available balance. If reducing the
+stake amount would take it below the pair's minimum tradeable amount, the trade is not opened at
+all, exactly as with other stake-sizing limits.
+
+This setting defaults to `1.0` (100%), which is equivalent to being disabled, since no single
+currency's exposure can ever exceed the total tradable capital.
+
+This setting applies identically to live/dry-run trading and to backtesting/hyperopt, so backtest
+results accurately reflect how the bot will behave live.
+
+``` json
+"max_currency_exposure": 0.2,
+```
+
 #### Amend last stake amount
 
 Assuming we have the tradable balance of 1000 USDT, `stake_amount=400`, and `max_open_trades=3`.
